body:
Similar to #1673 and #1674, type inference cannot determine the output of a call to `foo()` in following scenario:

```php
<?php

/** @psalm-template SomeType */
interface ParentType
{
    /** @psalm-return SomeType */
    function foo();
}

/** @psalm-template SomeOtherType */
interface ChildType extends ParentType
{
}

class ConcreteParameter
{
    function sayHello() : string
    {
        return 'hi';
    }
}

/**
 * @psalm-template RealObjectType as object
 *
 * @psalm-param class-string<RealObjectType> $className
 *
 * @psalm-return RealObjectType&ChildType<RealObjectType>&ParentType<RealObjectType>
 */
function makeConcrete(string $class) : object
{
    return new class() extends ConcreteParameter implements ChildType {
        public function foo() {
            return $this;
        }
    };
}

echo makeConcrete(ConcreteParameter::class)->foo()->sayHello();
```

This may be because of `ChildType` taking precedence over `ParentType` (just an assumption of mine).

https://psalm.dev/r/8178556639

